      "launcher.shortcut": "Open or close the dashboard: Alt+Shift+D (Mac: Option+Shift+D); close it with Esc as well",
      "launcher.ocr": "… from cover art",
      "launcher.ocrTitle": "Import the credits from the cover art (beta): the release's images, your own files or addresses are read first – their text is then the source; Discogs or Bandcamp can supplement it",
      "ocrStart.hint": "The import of this release has not started – the text read from the cover art will be its source.",
      "ms.2.16.0": "Status marks on every Discogs track line, each with the status of its track; “Directed By” is asked instead of assumed; columns can be taken out of the works matrix; column dates also go onto relationships MusicBrainz has without a date",
      "ms.2.17.0": "Choose the media before importing a release with several media; attributes (live, cover …) of the recording–work links in the works matrix, “live” preselected on live releases; “Music and lyrics by” → writer with “Song” preselected; the log can sit next to the edit note",
      "ms.2.18.0": "Works matrix in the look of the date matrix and more compact: column heads as cards, roles as chips, attributes (live, cover …) as short forms below each work; track groups can be dropped onto column heads, roles and attributes; track lists from the Discogs notes (“XYZ Publishing (1, 4, 6)”) as suggestions; “live” preselected only on new links",
      "ms.2.19.0": "Suggestions look the same everywhere: dashed and yellow (date matrix, works matrix, “li?”, entries from the Discogs notes not used yet in the pools); “Commissioned By” → commissioned on the works; “Live Recording By” → recording engineer and a hint for “live”",
      "ms.3.0.0": "Rebuilt inside: Discogs is read by a source adapter that delivers a neutral list of credits (person with links, role as written, details, tracks, source), and the rest of the script works only with that list. Nothing changes for you; it prepares other sources",
      "ms.3.3.0": "New name: Credits Importer (and Credits Importer Companion). Besides Discogs it reads Bandcamp albums (credits, also those of the track pages) and pasted texts (booklet, liner notes): names there are only suggested. A preference list per physical and digital media decides which linked source is loaded; for digital releases Bandcamp comes first",
      "ms.3.5.0": "Supplement with a second source, on request only: “Supplement with …” reads another linked source or a pasted text and lists what it adds (new roles, new entries) and where it differs, to take over by choice; rows it confirms get its mark. “Delete stored import …” starts the import of a release afresh. The Bandcamp spelling is shown next to the release’s artist credit and MusicBrainz. A fresh start: all stored data was reset once",
      "ms.3.10.0": "The rows of an entry rearrange with the width of the dashboard (relationship and attributes, level, date and tracks one above the other in a narrow window); a date from the pool or the matrix is a chip, its fields open with ✎, begin above end. Dates of the date matrix can be marked “Release level”. Texts: “tenor & soprano sax”, recording place and dates in Bandcamp’s “about” text, name suggestions without accents and with middle names; supplement with any Discogs or Bandcamp URL",
      "ms.3.15.0": "Works matrix: the tracks without a work are compared with all works of the release’s artists, its writers and its musicians – works linked to them and works of their recordings (also covers), in the background, read once per session; a large catalogue is named. Pasted texts and Bandcamp credits: credits in sentences (“Music played and recorded by … in September and October 2026”), “Role Name” lines and “… of this release were created by a human” (the release’s artists suggested) are recognized. Arrows in the status bar jump to the top or bottom of the dashboard",
      "ms.3.12.0": "Rebuilt inside: all mapping rules and word lists in one place of the script (the mapping register), the role rules as plain data. What the script makes of a source stays the same – checked with about 1,200 roles, 100 company roles, 50 date phrases and pasted texts. “Mapping rules” also lists the tables and word lists now (read only) and shows the right level for 27 rules (e.g. “Written-By”: work, “Artwork”: release)",
      "ms.2.14.0": "Works matrix: a date dropped onto a relationship already in MusicBrainz without a date is added to it (an edit); status marks also for credits of works that were new in the editor",
      "ms.2.13.0": "Track groups by drag & drop onto the tracks of rows; dates and track groups stay in the folded bar; status marks of work credits (composer, publisher) are checked on the works too",
      "ms.2.11.0": "After an update, a message shows the milestones of the new version",
      "ms.2.10.0": "Pool dates by drag & drop onto rows and onto each other (periods); pools load again from the Discogs notes",
      "ms.2.9.0": "The dashboard in the page as an alternative to the window",
      "ms.2.8.0": "Date matrix: dates in columns per date group, track groups on dates, applied with one button; “Dates & tracks” folds; all settings back to defaults",
      "ms.2.5.0": "Track pool: dates for some tracks, rows split by tracks and dates",
      "ms.2.4.0": "Dates found in free text and the Discogs notes, with date rules in the register",
      "ms.2.3.0": "Own mapping rules: create, switch any rule on or off, export and import",
      "ms.2.0.0": "Central mapping register for all Discogs → MusicBrainz rules, with the “Mapping rules” overview and test field",
      "ms.1.9.0": "Role credits added to relationships that already exist in MusicBrainz",
      "ms.1.7.0": "Discogs status marks on the Discogs page and navigation back to the dashboard",
      "ms.1.5.0": "Large releases: one medium at a time, loading media in the editor, staging in rounds",
      "ms.1.2.0": "Updating what was staged: coming back to the dashboard after “Stage”",
      "ms.1.1.0": "New works created in the relationship editor, like “Batch-add new works”, together with their writers and publishers",
      "ms.1.0.0": "Works matrix, date groups, publisher evidence and Discogs series",
      "ms.0.9.0": "Any MusicBrainz entry can be added by hand (artists, labels, places, series, events …)",
      "ms.0.7.0": "Relationships already in MusicBrainz are recognised and skipped",
      "ms.0.6.0": "Dates in MusicBrainz format with a date pool",
      "ms.0.5.0": "“Companies, etc.”: labels, studios and other places from Discogs",
      "ms.0.4.0": "Dashboard in English, German, Spanish and French",
      "ms.c0.1.0": "Discogs view: the Discogs tab shows where each credit comes from",
      "ms.0.3.0": "Works: linked works checked, existing works found, new works created",
      "ms.0.1.0": "First version: the credits of the linked Discogs release in the release relationship editor",
